# Release notes

Spec: [`docs/workflow/release-notes-workflow.md`](../../docs/workflow/release-notes-workflow.md). Procedure: skill `.cursor/skills/release-notes/SKILL.md`. Applies when the user mentions release notes, changelog, tagging or publishing (`session-abschluss` B/C).

## Rules

- **No release notes for `-dev.N` versions.** `scripts/release_notes_collect.py` refuses them; do not write a notes file for a dev version.
- **Git evidence baseline** = newest productive tag `vX.Y.Z` (never alpha / beta / rc / dev) that is an ancestor of `HEAD` and has a **published** (non-draft) GitHub Release — declined candidates are skipped (needs `gh`; otherwise pass `--since <tag>`). Productive tags released on a hotfix branch and not merged are listed as a warning in the evidence — do not announce their fixes as new.
- **Narrative baseline (draft prose)** = last **public** productive release the community runs (typically `:latest`, e.g. `2.6.2`) — **never** the previous alpha / beta / rc. Do not structure drafts as “delta since alpha.N”. Skill `release-notes` §1b.
- **The AI writes drafts only**, to `.github/release-notes/drafts/v<version>.draft.md`. Never write or overwrite `.github/release-notes/v<version>.md` directly, and never mark a draft as reviewed on the maintainer's behalf.
- **Review gate:** the maintainer reviews (edits the draft or requests changes). Only an explicit approval in chat ("Release Notes freigegeben") for that version lets the draft become `v<version>.md`. Approval does not carry over to later versions.
- Pre-release (alpha / beta / rc) notes: short, cumulative since the last **public** productive release, with the pre-release banner. Official notes: the full set.
- **Language:** German body for end users; only the Docker / deploy boilerplate stays English. First prose line = end-user sentence for the HA add-on Änderungsprotokoll (no pin / `latest` / channel jargon, no backlog IDs). Directly below it: a **very compact summary bullet list** (4–7 single-line items, ≤ ~10 words each, breaking/user-action first) — `bump_ha_addon` copies sentence + list into the Änderungsprotokoll.
- Visible text contains **no internal backlog version IDs (`2.7.n`, `2.6.a`, `2.+1`, `P5`, `Q8`) and no real user/customer names** (finalize and the CI gate reject `X.Y.<letter>` / `X.+N`; IDs belong only in `<!-- src: -->` comments) (`backlog-anonymize-users.mdc`). Maintainer hints from `.github/release-notes/UNRELEASED.md` must appear (breaking items first).
- Every statement must trace to the evidence pack; no invented features. Unclear items get a `<!-- REVIEW: … -->` marker, not a guess.
- New `MigrationStep`s since the baseline → `## Migration` section (`config-migration.mdc`, `python -m scripts.migration_release_notes --since <tag>`).
- Do not tag or publish with an unreviewed draft. The `version.py` rule stays: never change it without approval (`versioning.mdc`).
- **Audience:** backlog markers `[feat]` / `[qual]` / `[dev]` decide what is published (`backlog.mdc` §7, spec §8). `[feat]` -> Highlights / Neue Funktionen; `[qual]` -> short section "Qualität & Stabilität" (1–3 lines, no details); `[dev]` -> **never** in notes. Bugfixes -> "Verbesserungen & Korrekturen". Entries the evidence lists as *unmarked* must be clarified with the maintainer (ask), not guessed. `.github/release-notes/audience.toml` only pre-classifies.
